## Appendix C: The Pairing Matrix Relation

```
ratio = kL · (1 − 1/(kL + d))
```

For `d = 4`, `kL = 38.44251`:

```
ratio = 38.44251 · (1 − 1/42.44251)
      = 38.44251 · 0.97643
      = 37.536755
```

Observed ratio: `37.537200`. Relative error: `1.2 × 10⁻⁵`.

Solving for `kL` from the observed ratio:

```
kL² + kL·(d − 1 − ratio) − ratio·d = 0
```

For `d = 4`, `ratio = 37.5372`:

```
kL² − 34.5372·kL − 150.1488 = 0
kL = 38.442956
```

Actual `kL`: `38.44251`. Error: `1.2 × 10⁻⁵`.

